  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\nThe strategy leverages a more systematic exploration of initial guesses and improved numerical methods to escape local optima. By combining structured guesses with adaptive optimization, we aim to discover lower C\u2085 values than previously possible.\n\n2. Mathematical specification\nWe formulate the problem as a constrained optimization:\n\nMinimize: max_k [ dx * sum_{i=0}^{n-1} h[i]*(1 - h[i+k mod 2n-1]) ]\n\nSubject to:\n- 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1, \u2200i\n- sum(h) = n_points / 2\n\n3. Implementation procedure\nA. Generate initial guesses using combinations of triangular, sawtooth, and square waves.\nB. Use adaptive perturbations with decreasing step size.\nC. Apply SLSQP with dynamic stopping criteria.\nD. Enforce constraints using a projection operator.\nE. Track the best solution, ensuring feasibility at each step.\n\n4. Search choices and useful variations\nInitialization strategies:\n- Waveform combinations\n- Adaptive perturbation sizes\n- Different optimizers\n\n5. Compute budget and robustness\nThe approach is designed to fit within the time budget by monitoring progress and terminating ineffective searches early.\n\n6. Validation and return contract\nFinal solutions are validated for feasibility and objective consistency before returning.",
